# Cortex instance configuration — sourced by the harness (bash).
#
# Copy to `factory.config` and edit for your machine. This file holds NO secrets — agent keys live
# in ~/.config/buzz/agents/ and never here.
#
# Cortex is the operator for your Synapse standing agents. It assumes you have installed, separately:
#   - Block's Buzz (Apache-2.0) built at $BUZZ_REPO  (relay + buzz-acp + buzz + buzz-admin)
#   - @eborja/synapse in your vault                  (the engine + the synapse-mcp server)
#   - an ACP runtime on PATH                         (claude-agent-acp, or cursor-agent)

# ── Paths (this instance's identity — assigned directly, NOT ${VAR:-…} on purpose) ─────
# These define which vault/relay/identity this instance drives. Hard-assigned so a stray exported
# $SYNAPSE_VAULT in your shell cannot silently redirect the whole harness to another vault. Edit them.
SYNAPSE_VAULT="$HOME/synapse/synapse-vault"                      # vault the agents brief from
BUZZ_REPO="$HOME/synapse/buzz"                                   # your built Block/Buzz checkout
BUZZ_OWNER_ENV="$HOME/.config/buzz/agents/owner.env"            # your Buzz identity (admin ops)

# ── Relay / channel ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
BUZZ_DEFAULT_CHANNEL_NAME="${BUZZ_DEFAULT_CHANNEL_NAME:-general}"

# ── Defaults (per-agent settings below can override) ────────────────────────────
BUZZ_SYNAPSE_AGENT_COMMAND="${BUZZ_SYNAPSE_AGENT_COMMAND:-claude-agent-acp}"  # ACP runtime
SYNAPSE_MCP_SURFACE="${SYNAPSE_MCP_SURFACE:-full}"                            # default MCP surface
PROMPT_SOURCE="${PROMPT_SOURCE:-render}"   # render → `synapse render`; file → prompts/<agent>.system.md
# A standing agent answers on its own initiative, so its model is a STANDING cost. Defaults to the
# cheaper mid-tier; `default` defers to the runtime. List ids: buzz-acp models --agent-command <runtime>
MODEL="${MODEL:-sonnet}"                   # global default; AGENT_<name>_MODEL overrides per agent
RELAY_OBSERVER="${RELAY_OBSERVER:-1}"      # publish ACP observer frames → the client's Activity panel
# Observer frames are encrypted TO THE OWNER, so RELAY_OBSERVER alone publishes nothing. Defaults to the
# pubkey in BUZZ_OWNER_ENV. Set this when you WATCH from a different identity than you run admin ops
# from — a desktop app and the CLI are separate pubkeys, and frames encrypted to one are unreadable
# by the other.
# AGENT_OWNER="<64-char hex pubkey of the client you watch from>"

# ── Roster: the agents this instance runs ───────────────────────────────────────
# DERIVED by default from the vault: every agent whose definition declares `addressable: true`
# (synapse decision-0008) gets an identity and a process. Leave this unset — the package owns the
# roster, so a new watchable agent needs a vault edit, not a harness edit.
# Uncomment only to deliberately override, e.g. a test instance running a subset:
# STANDING=(oracle curator)

# ── Per-agent behaviour (optional; defaults apply when unset) ────────────────────
# Flat vars named AGENT_<name>_<FIELD> (no associative arrays — macOS bash 3.2 lacks them):
#   AGENT_<name>_HUB      the hub the agent briefs on            → `synapse render <agent> <hub>`
#   AGENT_<name>_PROFILE  render profile: lean | standard | fat
#   AGENT_<name>_SURFACE  MCP surface for THAT agent: skeleton | standard | full
#                         (run oracle on `standard` so the read front door cannot mutate — the
#                          create_* tools live on `full` only, enforced by the surface not a prompt)
#   AGENT_<name>_RUNTIME  override the ACP runtime for one agent
AGENT_oracle_HUB="hub-projects";  AGENT_oracle_PROFILE="standard";  AGENT_oracle_SURFACE="standard"
AGENT_curator_HUB="hub-synapse";  AGENT_curator_PROFILE="standard"; AGENT_curator_SURFACE="full"
